1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:24,000
I would like, if I may, this evening,

2
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:44,000
to talk about the implications of meditation

3
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,680
and what is necessary for a mind

4
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:58,560
that is capable of really true meditation.

5
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:05,800
What is the first step, as it were?

6
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:12,800
First of all,

7
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:18,800
I think one has to understand

8
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:24,800
the meaning of the word freedom.

9
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:35,800
For most of us,

10
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:44,800
freedom implies freedom to express ourselves,

11
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:53,800
or freedom to do what we like in society,

12
00:01:54,800 --> 00:02:00,800
or freedom to think what we like,

13
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:08,800
or freedom from a particular tiresome habit,

14
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:18,800
or a particular idiosyncrasy, and so on.

15
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:24,800
To understand what is freedom,

16
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:30,800
because that is, it seems to be absolutely necessary

17
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:38,800
for a mind that is capable, without any distortion,

18
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:45,800
to be able to meditate.

19
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:52,800
Now, for most of us,

20
00:02:52,800 --> 00:03:01,800
we demand freedom politically, or religiously,

21
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:05,800
or to think what we like,

22
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:12,800
and there is the freedom of choice.

23
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:30,800
Political freedom is all right, and one must have it.

24
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:36,800
But for most of us, we never demand and find out

25
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:42,800
whether it is at all possible to be free inwardly.

26
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:51,800
Our mind is a slave to its own projections,

27
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:55,800
to its own demands,

28
00:03:55,800 --> 00:04:00,800
to its own desires and fulfilments.

29
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:09,800
The mind is a slave to its cravings,

30
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:13,800
to its appetites.

31
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:17,800
And apparently we never ask

32
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:24,800
whether it is at all possible to be free inwardly.

33
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:30,800
But we are always wanting freedom outwardly,

34
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:35,800
to go against the society,

35
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:42,800
against a particular structure of society.

36
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:51,800
And this revolt against society,

37
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:55,800
which is taking place all over the world,

38
00:04:57,800 --> 00:05:01,800
is a form of violence

39
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:07,800
which indicates that one is concentrating

40
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:16,800
on an outward change, without the inward change.

41
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:30,800
So, violence plays an extraordinary part in our life.

42
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:35,800
We never ask whether the mind can be completely

43
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:40,800
and utterly free from violence.

44
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:44,800
We have accepted it as part of life,

45
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:50,800
as we have accepted war as the way of life.

46
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:56,800
And we have our favourite wars.

47
00:05:57,800 --> 00:06:01,800
You may not like this particular war,

48
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:07,800
but you don't mind having other kinds of wars.

49
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:16,800
And there will be always wars,

50
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:22,800
and there have been for five thousand years wars,

51
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:29,800
because man has accepted violence as the way of life.

52
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:35,800
And we never question whether the mind can be really

53
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:42,800
and truly, deeply, be free of violence.

54
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:55,800
And the permissive society in which we live,

55
00:06:55,800 --> 00:07:03,800
the culture in which it is gradually coming out of this society,

56
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:13,800
to do what one likes, or choose what one likes,

57
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:18,800
is still an indication of violence.

58
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:24,800
Where there is choice, there is no freedom.

59
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:32,800
Choice implies confusion, not clarity.

60
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:38,800
When you see something very clearly, there is no choice,

61
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:41,800
there is only action.

62
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:46,800
It is only a confused mind that chooses.

63
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:55,800
And choice is an indication of the lack of freedom.

64
00:07:56,800 --> 00:08:03,800
And therefore in choice there is resistance, conflict.

65
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:16,800
And so our life as it is now is based on violence.

66
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:23,800
Our life is conditioned by the verb to be.

67
00:08:26,800 --> 00:08:34,800
Please, this is important to understand

68
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:46,800
how our life is guided and conditioned by the verb to be.

69
00:08:46,800 --> 00:08:55,800
One has been, one is, and one will be.

70
00:08:57,800 --> 00:09:04,800
The idea in that verb is to arrive, to succeed,

71
00:09:04,800 --> 00:09:08,800
to achieve, to become,

72
00:09:08,800 --> 00:09:15,800
to gradually attain peace,

73
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:24,800
gradually get rid of the things that hinder us.

74
00:09:24,800 --> 00:09:35,800
So the verb to be is the conditioning of the mind in time.

75
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:39,800
Right?

76
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:43,800
Do please follow this.

77
00:09:46,800 --> 00:09:54,800
Because enlightenment is not a matter of time at all.

78
00:09:55,800 --> 00:10:06,800
Understanding is not a matter of gradual sensitivity.

79
00:10:08,800 --> 00:10:14,800
Either one understands it immediately or not at all.

80
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:23,800
And as long as the mind is conditioned by that verb,

81
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:29,800
and as most minds are,

82
00:10:29,800 --> 00:10:35,800
all our moral structure is based on that.

83
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:40,800
I will be good,

84
00:10:42,800 --> 00:10:49,800
I will gradually achieve a certain state of mind,

85
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:52,800
and so on.

86
00:10:54,800 --> 00:11:04,800
So, one has to be aware of this dangerous word,

87
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:15,800
and find out whether the mind can be free of word,

88
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:19,800
because the word is never the thing,

89
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:24,800
the description is never the described,

90
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:29,800
and yet we are satisfied with the description,

91
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:33,800
with the explanations.

92
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:44,800
So, as I said,

93
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:49,800
we are going to go into this question

94
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:54,800
of not only what is meditation,

95
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:59,800
and I believe that is a new word

96
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:06,800
that you have learnt in this country, brought from the East.

97
00:12:08,800 --> 00:12:14,800
And one doesn't know the full meaning of that word.

98
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:18,800
But before we go into that,

99
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:23,800
which is a very complex and the most important thing, meditation,

100
00:12:23,800 --> 00:12:26,800
it is the most beautiful thing in life,

101
00:12:26,800 --> 00:12:29,800
if you know what meditation is.

102
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:33,800
But before one can meditate,

103
00:12:33,800 --> 00:12:37,800
one must understand what is living,

104
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:42,800
what is love, and what is death.

105
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:44,800
If you don't understand that,

106
00:12:44,800 --> 00:12:49,800
your meditation is merely an escape,

107
00:12:49,800 --> 00:12:54,800
is a form of self-hypnosis.

108
00:12:55,800 --> 00:12:58,800
Right?

109
00:12:59,800 --> 00:13:03,800
So you must lay the foundation.

110
00:13:06,800 --> 00:13:10,800
Not gradually,

111
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:14,800
there must be order,

112
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:19,800
for the mind can fully comprehend

113
00:13:19,800 --> 00:13:24,800
the significance of what meditation is.

114
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:29,800
There must be complete order,

115
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:35,800
which means the end of all conflict,

116
00:13:35,800 --> 00:13:38,800
all disturbance,

117
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:45,800
all disorder within oneself.

118
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:50,800
Otherwise you are sitting down in a corner by yourself

119
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:53,800
for ten minutes a day,

120
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:56,800
and thinking you are going to meditate

121
00:13:56,800 --> 00:14:00,800
or achieve enlightenment is nonsense,

122
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:04,800
if you don't mind my saying so.

123
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:07,800
Right?

124
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:12,800
So one has to understand what living is.

125
00:14:14,800 --> 00:14:18,800
And one can understand that only

126
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:24,800
by observing what actually it is,

127
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:35,800
not in opposition to a concept,

128
00:14:36,800 --> 00:14:40,800
to a formula, to an ideology,

129
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:44,800
but actually what it is.

130
00:14:45,800 --> 00:14:53,800
So one must be free to observe actually what our life is.

131
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:59,800
Not what it should be.

132
00:15:01,800 --> 00:15:06,800
If you are thinking in terms of what it should be,

133
00:15:06,800 --> 00:15:13,800
then you are totally avoiding what actual life is.

134
00:15:16,800 --> 00:15:22,800
So what is this life that we are living?

135
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:32,800
This life, the actual daily life, is disorder.

136
00:15:35,800 --> 00:15:38,800
Isn't it?

137
00:15:39,800 --> 00:15:42,800
There is conflict,

138
00:15:43,800 --> 00:15:48,800
there is driving ambition,

139
00:15:49,800 --> 00:15:56,800
there is battle in ourselves,

140
00:15:58,800 --> 00:16:04,800
opposing contradictory desires and wills,

141
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:11,800
endless frustrations.

142
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:16,800
And there is frustration

143
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:20,800
because we have never understood what fulfilment is,

144
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:24,800
and if there is such a thing as fulfilment.

145
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:30,800
What is there to fulfil?

146
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:34,800
One's own particular little ambition,

147
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:40,800
one's own appetites, envies,

148
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:44,800
ambitions to be somebody,

149
00:16:45,800 --> 00:16:53,800
and what is it, that centre that demands all this,

150
00:16:54,800 --> 00:17:02,800
is not that very centre the cause of disorder?

151
00:17:04,800 --> 00:17:09,800
And without bringing about order in that life,

152
00:17:09,800 --> 00:17:13,800
complete mathematical order,

153
00:17:14,800 --> 00:17:17,800
there is no order.

154
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:24,800
Life has very little meaning.

155
00:17:26,800 --> 00:17:31,800
Going to the office every day for the rest of the 60 years,

156
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:34,800
or 40 years,

157
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:38,800
living in this constant battle

158
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:42,800
between what is and what should be,

159
00:17:43,800 --> 00:17:48,800
between the frustrated ambitions

160
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:55,800
and the simple, clear, beautiful life,

161
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:04,800
the images that one has built about oneself and about others,

162
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:11,800
the self-centred activity that is going on all the time,

163
00:18:11,800 --> 00:18:15,800
which is isolating each one,

164
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:21,800
and therefore dividing.

165
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:26,800
And that's our life, a life of conflict,

166
00:18:26,800 --> 00:18:32,800
a life that has really no meaning as it is,

167
00:18:36,800 --> 00:18:40,800
a life that is a battlefield,

168
00:18:40,800 --> 00:18:47,800
not only in yourself but also in your relationship,

169
00:18:47,800 --> 00:18:56,800
a life of division, contradiction, routine, monotonous,

170
00:18:57,800 --> 00:19:02,800
and a life that is, when you look at it very deeply,

171
00:19:02,800 --> 00:19:05,800
utterly lonely,

172
00:19:06,800 --> 00:19:11,800
a life that has no beauty.

173
00:19:13,800 --> 00:19:16,800
And that is our life.

174
00:19:16,800 --> 00:19:20,800
And we are not exaggerating it.

175
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:25,800
If you observe yourself very carefully,

176
00:19:25,800 --> 00:19:30,800
without any prejudice, bias,

177
00:19:31,800 --> 00:19:37,800
when you look at every human being right through the world,

178
00:19:38,800 --> 00:19:42,800
the saint, the priest,

179
00:19:43,800 --> 00:19:47,800
the specialist, the careerist,

180
00:19:47,800 --> 00:19:50,800
the ordinary layman,

181
00:19:50,800 --> 00:19:54,800
are all caught in this.

182
00:19:54,800 --> 00:20:04,800
And we want to escape from it.

183
00:20:07,800 --> 00:20:12,800
And so you escape through nationalism,

184
00:20:15,800 --> 00:20:20,800
through beliefs, through dogmas,

185
00:20:21,800 --> 00:20:26,800
through innumerable forms of entertainment,

186
00:20:27,800 --> 00:20:32,800
in which is included the religious entertainment.

187
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:37,800
That's our life.

188
00:20:41,800 --> 00:20:47,800
Comparing ourselves with something that should be,

189
00:20:47,800 --> 00:20:51,800
comparing ourselves with the greater, with the nobler,

190
00:20:51,800 --> 00:20:54,800
with the more intelligent, with the more spiritual,

191
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:57,800
and so on and on and on,

192
00:20:57,800 --> 00:21:01,800
and therefore conflict and fear.

193
00:21:02,800 --> 00:21:05,800
This is our life.

194
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:11,800
A battle for security,

195
00:21:12,800 --> 00:21:15,800
and in the very search of security,

196
00:21:15,800 --> 00:21:18,800
psychological as well as physical,

197
00:21:18,800 --> 00:21:22,800
we bring about destruction.

198
00:21:25,800 --> 00:21:30,800
These are obvious facts.

199
00:21:34,800 --> 00:21:40,800
And from this we want to escape,

200
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:43,800
because man has lived like this

201
00:21:43,800 --> 00:21:48,800
for thousands and thousands of years,

202
00:21:48,800 --> 00:21:57,800
with sorrow, confusion, and great misery and mischief.

203
00:22:00,800 --> 00:22:05,800
And without changing all that,

204
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:10,800
completely, radically,

205
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:20,800
a mere outward revolution,

206
00:22:21,800 --> 00:22:27,800
changing a particular system for another system,

207
00:22:27,800 --> 00:22:34,800
does not solve this aching agony.

208
00:22:34,800 --> 00:22:42,800
There is only one revolution,

209
00:22:43,800 --> 00:22:47,800
the inward revolution.

210
00:22:51,800 --> 00:22:59,800
So, spitting on society,

211
00:22:59,800 --> 00:23:05,800
blaming society for your condition,

212
00:23:06,800 --> 00:23:13,800
is obviously blaming something which you have created.

213
00:23:14,800 --> 00:23:20,800
It's your society, you have built it

214
00:23:21,800 --> 00:23:28,800
by your greed, envy, ambition, competitiveness, comparison,

215
00:23:28,800 --> 00:23:34,800
by one's own inward hatreds, violence.

216
00:23:35,800 --> 00:23:40,800
So that is our life,

217
00:23:41,800 --> 00:23:46,800
really quite insane life.

218
00:23:50,800 --> 00:23:55,800
Now, the question is,

219
00:23:55,800 --> 00:24:00,800
how can that life be changed?

220
00:24:02,800 --> 00:24:10,800
Not gradually, but immediately,

221
00:24:10,800 --> 00:24:18,800
otherwise you are sowing the seed of violence.

222
00:24:18,800 --> 00:24:20,800
Though you may want peace,

223
00:24:20,800 --> 00:24:30,800
you are actually sowing the seeds of enmity, misery.

224
00:24:30,800 --> 00:24:39,800
So, seeing all this, non-verbally,

225
00:24:41,800 --> 00:24:45,800
not as an explanation,

226
00:24:46,800 --> 00:24:49,800
not as an idea,

227
00:24:49,800 --> 00:24:53,800
but seeing it actually as it is,

228
00:24:53,800 --> 00:24:59,800
feeling it as you feel hunger,

229
00:25:01,800 --> 00:25:06,800
therefore being intimately related to it.

230
00:25:08,800 --> 00:25:13,800
And you cannot be deeply,

231
00:25:14,800 --> 00:25:19,800
beautifully related to this living,

232
00:25:20,800 --> 00:25:22,800
which we call life,

233
00:25:22,800 --> 00:25:28,800
as long as you have any form of escape from it,

234
00:25:30,800 --> 00:25:34,800
any form of distortion.

235
00:25:35,800 --> 00:25:51,800
So, awareness without choice,

236
00:25:52,800 --> 00:25:59,800
to be aware of this whole phenomenon of existence,

237
00:26:00,800 --> 00:26:03,800
not someone else's existence,

238
00:26:03,800 --> 00:26:10,800
not being aware of our life according to somebody,

239
00:26:10,800 --> 00:26:16,800
some philosopher, some guru, some psychologist,

240
00:26:16,800 --> 00:26:21,800
but being aware of it actually,

241
00:26:21,800 --> 00:26:26,800
because you yourself see it.

242
00:26:33,800 --> 00:26:42,800
If one is so completely aware of it, and one must,

243
00:26:44,800 --> 00:26:51,800
because one cannot possibly live as we are living.

244
00:26:55,800 --> 00:27:00,800
We are talking inwardly, psychologically,

245
00:27:00,800 --> 00:27:04,800
a life that is so torn.

246
00:27:09,800 --> 00:27:14,800
And if we want order,

247
00:27:16,800 --> 00:27:20,800
and order is virtue,

248
00:27:21,800 --> 00:27:26,800
order demands discipline,

249
00:27:26,800 --> 00:27:33,800
that is, to learn, not to conform, not to imitate,

250
00:27:33,800 --> 00:27:36,800
but to learn,

251
00:27:36,800 --> 00:27:42,800
and to learn about the disorder, which is our life,

252
00:27:42,800 --> 00:27:46,800
to observe it, to learn.

253
00:27:47,800 --> 00:27:54,800
And in that observation comes an extraordinary discipline,

254
00:27:55,800 --> 00:27:59,800
not imposed by anybody,

255
00:28:00,800 --> 00:28:10,800
because the very observation itself has its own discipline,

256
00:28:15,800 --> 00:28:20,800
in the very act of observing your learning,

257
00:28:20,800 --> 00:28:23,800
and therefore the learning is the discipline.

258
00:28:24,800 --> 00:28:28,800
Please do see this because

259
00:28:29,800 --> 00:28:36,800
we have imposed upon ourselves so many disciplines,

260
00:28:37,800 --> 00:28:40,800
the business discipline, the religious discipline,

261
00:28:40,800 --> 00:28:43,800
the family discipline.

262
00:28:43,800 --> 00:28:49,800
Of course, a military discipline is the most absurd kind of discipline.

263
00:28:53,800 --> 00:29:00,800
But we have got so many disciplines,

264
00:29:00,800 --> 00:29:04,800
the must and the must-nots,

265
00:29:04,800 --> 00:29:10,800
always conforming, imitating, suppressing,

266
00:29:10,800 --> 00:29:16,800
and being suppressed, wanting to fulfil.

267
00:29:18,800 --> 00:29:22,800
All that is disorder.

268
00:29:24,800 --> 00:29:33,800
So to understand order, to learn about order,

269
00:29:33,800 --> 00:29:37,800
not what order should be,

270
00:29:37,800 --> 00:29:45,800
but to learn about it, one must learn about disorder.

271
00:29:45,800 --> 00:29:47,800
Right?

272
00:29:47,800 --> 00:29:51,800
Are we following each other?

273
00:29:52,800 --> 00:29:59,800
Or are you being slowly, being mesmerised by words?

274
00:30:02,800 --> 00:30:07,800
Well, if you are, t'en opi, it's up to you.

275
00:30:09,800 --> 00:30:15,800
We said one must learn about disorder,

276
00:30:16,800 --> 00:30:19,800
which is our life, which is our mind,

277
00:30:19,800 --> 00:30:26,800
our heart, our very core of our being is disorder.

278
00:30:28,800 --> 00:30:31,800
Because if you say there is a soul,

279
00:30:31,800 --> 00:30:35,800
there is, according to the Hindus, the Atman and so on,

280
00:30:35,800 --> 00:30:39,800
they are just theories.

281
00:30:41,800 --> 00:30:46,800
Philosophy has nothing to do with living.

282
00:30:46,800 --> 00:30:51,800
And we are trying to understand what living is.

283
00:30:51,800 --> 00:30:56,800
And we see in that living there is disorder, utter disorder,

284
00:30:56,800 --> 00:30:59,800
the battle, the misery, the confusion,

285
00:30:59,800 --> 00:31:05,800
the agony, the guilt, the fear.

286
00:31:07,800 --> 00:31:12,800
So one has to observe without any choice

287
00:31:12,800 --> 00:31:18,800
this disorder which is you, which is me.

288
00:31:19,800 --> 00:31:25,800
To observe it, not what you want it to be.

289
00:31:29,800 --> 00:31:34,800
Then you create conflict between what is and what should be.

290
00:31:34,800 --> 00:31:39,800
And where there is conflict there is disorder.

291
00:31:39,800 --> 00:31:43,800
Please do understand this thing very simply.

292
00:31:43,800 --> 00:31:46,800
Once you understand this you will find

293
00:31:46,800 --> 00:31:50,800
that by observing disorder in oneself,

294
00:31:50,800 --> 00:31:53,800
without any distortion,

295
00:31:53,800 --> 00:31:59,800
without wanting to bring about order out of this disorder,

296
00:32:01,800 --> 00:32:06,800
trying to impose what you think is order upon disorder,

297
00:32:06,800 --> 00:32:13,800
but observe it without any choice, without any distortion.

298
00:32:13,800 --> 00:32:20,800
Then out of that observation comes supreme order,

299
00:32:20,800 --> 00:32:24,800
the highest good.

300
00:32:28,800 --> 00:32:35,800
And in that there is a total revolution

301
00:32:37,800 --> 00:32:42,800
and from that inward, radical change

302
00:32:42,800 --> 00:32:47,800
then there comes outward order, not the other way round.

303
00:32:47,800 --> 00:32:52,800
We want outward order first.

304
00:32:53,800 --> 00:32:57,800
And it has never been possible.

305
00:32:57,800 --> 00:33:01,800
Every revolution, including the Communist revolution,

306
00:33:01,800 --> 00:33:04,800
said, forget about the inward order,

307
00:33:04,800 --> 00:33:09,800
let's have state order.

308
00:33:10,800 --> 00:33:12,800
And you know what is happening.

309
00:33:12,800 --> 00:33:15,800
Every revolution has done this,

310
00:33:15,800 --> 00:33:19,800
tried to bring about outward order,

311
00:33:19,800 --> 00:33:23,800
without paying any attention whatsoever

312
00:33:23,800 --> 00:33:29,800
to the psychological supreme order within oneself.

313
00:33:34,800 --> 00:33:44,800
And order means also not only virtue but love.

314
00:33:44,800 --> 00:33:48,800
And what is love?

315
00:33:52,800 --> 00:33:56,800
I wonder if you have ever asked that question,

316
00:33:56,800 --> 00:34:00,800
what love is.

317
00:34:00,800 --> 00:34:03,800
Have you?

318
00:34:04,800 --> 00:34:09,800
What is love?

319
00:34:09,800 --> 00:34:13,800
How will you find out?

320
00:34:14,800 --> 00:34:23,800
Only you will find out what it is through what it is not.

321
00:34:25,800 --> 00:34:30,800
Through negation the positive comes.

322
00:34:30,800 --> 00:34:34,800
But if you pursue the positive,

323
00:34:34,800 --> 00:34:42,800
then it is the pursuit of the projection of the mind.

324
00:34:43,800 --> 00:34:48,800
So when you deny all the projections of the mind

325
00:34:48,800 --> 00:34:55,800
by denying in a sense, setting it aside, negating,

326
00:34:56,800 --> 00:34:59,800
then you will find out what it is.

327
00:35:01,800 --> 00:35:06,800
So that's what we are going to do.

328
00:35:08,800 --> 00:35:16,800
Find out what it is not, to find out what it is.

329
00:35:17,800 --> 00:35:22,800
Is this... can we go on? Right.

330
00:35:23,800 --> 00:35:28,800
We said, what is love?

331
00:35:29,800 --> 00:35:36,800
You know, that's one of the most important things in life.

332
00:35:38,800 --> 00:35:43,800
If one has love you can do what you like,

333
00:35:43,800 --> 00:35:46,800
then there is no conflict,

334
00:35:46,800 --> 00:35:50,800
then there is no evil.

335
00:35:51,800 --> 00:35:57,800
There is great bliss.

336
00:35:59,800 --> 00:36:08,800
But to imagine what bliss is and pursue that is not love.

337
00:36:10,800 --> 00:36:14,800
So we are going to see what it is not

338
00:36:14,800 --> 00:36:19,800
and therefore come upon what it is.

339
00:36:21,800 --> 00:36:26,800
Therefore it is not a question of searching out love,

340
00:36:27,800 --> 00:36:30,800
nor cultivating love.

341
00:36:31,800 --> 00:36:34,800
How can you cultivate love?

342
00:36:34,800 --> 00:36:40,800
All cultivation is the product of the mind,

343
00:36:40,800 --> 00:36:44,800
product of thought.

344
00:36:45,800 --> 00:36:50,800
It is like a mind that pursues humility.

345
00:36:51,800 --> 00:36:57,800
It says, I know vanity and I must cultivate humility.

346
00:36:57,800 --> 00:37:03,800
And when a mind that is proud and vain cultivates humility,

347
00:37:03,800 --> 00:37:06,800
it is still vain.

348
00:37:07,800 --> 00:37:14,800
It is like those saints that are pretending to be humble

349
00:37:14,800 --> 00:37:19,800
because they have cultivated humility.

350
00:37:21,800 --> 00:37:28,800
So what we are going to do is to find out what it is not.

351
00:37:29,800 --> 00:37:34,800
Not through me, not through the speaker at all,

352
00:37:35,800 --> 00:37:41,800
but by listening to yourself

353
00:37:41,800 --> 00:37:44,800
and finding out what it is not,

354
00:37:44,800 --> 00:37:50,800
and if it is not that, to wipe it away instantly.

355
00:37:51,800 --> 00:37:56,800
If you don't wipe it, if it doesn't disappear,

356
00:37:56,800 --> 00:37:58,800
then you are caught.

357
00:37:58,800 --> 00:38:05,800
At the time you are a slave to the word and the verb to be,

358
00:38:06,800 --> 00:38:10,800
and therefore there is no love.

359
00:38:14,800 --> 00:38:20,800
So first we are asking what it is not.

360
00:38:20,800 --> 00:38:26,800
Obviously it is not jealousy.

361
00:38:28,800 --> 00:38:32,800
It is not envy.

362
00:38:39,800 --> 00:38:44,800
And your love is hedged about,

363
00:38:44,800 --> 00:38:51,800
a prisoner to jealousy, envy.

364
00:38:52,800 --> 00:38:54,800
Right?

365
00:38:55,800 --> 00:39:00,800
And when you see that, what you call love

366
00:39:00,800 --> 00:39:06,800
is entangled with the ugly brutality of jealousy,

367
00:39:06,800 --> 00:39:10,800
see it, actually observe it.

368
00:39:12,800 --> 00:39:17,800
And in that observation, jealousy goes,

369
00:39:17,800 --> 00:39:21,800
and you will never be jealous again,

370
00:39:21,800 --> 00:39:24,800
never envious.

371
00:39:29,800 --> 00:39:33,800
Please do this as we are talking.

372
00:39:33,800 --> 00:39:38,800
Envy comes only when there is comparison.

373
00:39:41,800 --> 00:39:45,800
And is love comparison?

374
00:39:46,800 --> 00:39:54,800
So, again, you put aside all comparison,

375
00:39:54,800 --> 00:39:57,800
which means all envy.

376
00:40:02,800 --> 00:40:07,800
Then is love pleasure?

377
00:40:08,800 --> 00:40:12,800
This is going to be a little more difficult.

378
00:40:13,800 --> 00:40:20,800
For most of us love is pleasure.

379
00:40:23,800 --> 00:40:28,800
Whether it is love, sexual love, or love of God,

380
00:40:28,800 --> 00:40:32,800
or love of God knows what else.

381
00:40:32,800 --> 00:40:36,800
It is based on pleasure,

382
00:40:37,800 --> 00:40:41,800
the love of respectability,

383
00:40:42,800 --> 00:40:48,800
is the very essence of the bourgeois mind.

384
00:40:50,800 --> 00:40:56,800
So, is love pleasure?

385
00:41:06,800 --> 00:41:10,800
Do observe it, please.

386
00:41:10,800 --> 00:41:15,800
We were saying yesterday evening what pleasure is,

387
00:41:15,800 --> 00:41:19,800
the product of thought.

388
00:41:21,800 --> 00:41:24,800
Having had pleasure of different kinds,

389
00:41:24,800 --> 00:41:30,800
yesterday you think about it,

390
00:41:30,800 --> 00:41:35,800
you have image upon image built,

391
00:41:35,800 --> 00:41:38,800
and that stimulates you,

392
00:41:38,800 --> 00:41:42,800
and that gives you pleasure, sexual or otherwise,

393
00:41:42,800 --> 00:41:45,800
and that you call love.

394
00:41:45,800 --> 00:41:48,800
And is it love?

395
00:41:48,800 --> 00:41:51,800
Because in pleasure there is frustration,

396
00:41:51,800 --> 00:41:57,800
there is pain, there is agony, there is dependency.

397
00:42:00,800 --> 00:42:06,800
Don't you depend psychologically on another?

398
00:42:09,800 --> 00:42:12,800
And when you do,

399
00:42:12,800 --> 00:42:16,800
when you depend on your wife or your husband, whatever it is,

400
00:42:16,800 --> 00:42:19,800
and you say, I love you,

401
00:42:19,800 --> 00:42:22,800
is that love?

402
00:42:24,800 --> 00:42:29,800
And in that dependence is there not fear?

403
00:42:30,800 --> 00:42:33,800
You are the product of your conditioning,

404
00:42:33,800 --> 00:42:36,800
you are the product of your society,

405
00:42:36,800 --> 00:42:40,800
you are the product of propaganda, religious and otherwise.

406
00:42:40,800 --> 00:42:43,800
For 2,000 years, as in India,

407
00:42:43,800 --> 00:42:47,800
10,000 or 5,000 years, they have been told

408
00:42:49,800 --> 00:42:53,800
what to believe, what to think.

409
00:42:56,800 --> 00:43:00,800
You repeat what others have said.

410
00:43:01,800 --> 00:43:04,800
All your education is that,

411
00:43:04,800 --> 00:43:08,800
a repetition of what you have learnt from a book.

412
00:43:15,800 --> 00:43:19,800
And you are that, you are conditioned.

413
00:43:21,800 --> 00:43:28,800
You are not free, happy, vital, passionate human beings.

414
00:43:29,800 --> 00:43:34,800
You are frightened human beings and therefore second-hand.

415
00:43:35,800 --> 00:43:39,800
You are full of authority of others,

416
00:43:39,800 --> 00:43:42,800
or your own particular little authority,

417
00:43:42,800 --> 00:43:45,800
of your own knowledge, you know something about something

418
00:43:45,800 --> 00:43:48,800
and you become an authority.

419
00:43:49,800 --> 00:43:52,800
So you are not free.

420
00:43:53,800 --> 00:43:58,800
And intellectually look, are you free?

421
00:44:00,800 --> 00:44:04,800
Not repeat what others have said,

422
00:44:06,800 --> 00:44:10,800
not what you have been taught in the university

423
00:44:10,800 --> 00:44:14,800
or what you have learnt from a book.

424
00:44:14,800 --> 00:44:17,800
And what have you experienced?

425
00:44:18,800 --> 00:44:22,800
Go into it, you will see what you have experienced.

426
00:44:26,800 --> 00:44:31,800
You have experienced something that you can always recognise,

427
00:44:32,800 --> 00:44:35,800
otherwise it is not an experience.

428
00:44:36,800 --> 00:44:40,800
Therefore your experience is not a experience.

429
00:44:40,800 --> 00:44:43,800
Therefore your experience is always old,

430
00:44:43,800 --> 00:44:47,800
like thought is always old, thought is never new,

431
00:44:50,800 --> 00:44:53,800
because it is the response of memory.

432
00:44:53,800 --> 00:44:57,800
So you, if you will forgive my repeating it,

433
00:44:57,800 --> 00:45:01,800
you are second-hand human beings,

434
00:45:02,800 --> 00:45:06,800
intellectually, emotionally.

435
00:45:06,800 --> 00:45:10,800
You go to places to learn how to be sensitive.

436
00:45:12,800 --> 00:45:15,800
Lovely idea, isn't it?

437
00:45:17,800 --> 00:45:21,800
Be taught by another how to think.

438
00:45:24,800 --> 00:45:27,800
So, morally,

439
00:45:30,800 --> 00:45:33,800
you are not free.

440
00:45:33,800 --> 00:45:36,800
You are not free.

441
00:45:39,800 --> 00:45:41,800
Intellectually,

442
00:45:43,800 --> 00:45:46,800
deeply, you are not free,

443
00:45:46,800 --> 00:45:51,800
and therefore you are only free in your sexual expression.

444
00:45:51,800 --> 00:45:56,800
And that is why it has become so extraordinarily important.

445
00:45:57,800 --> 00:46:00,800
There you are full,

446
00:46:04,800 --> 00:46:06,800
there you are free,

447
00:46:06,800 --> 00:46:08,800
though it has its own problems

448
00:46:08,800 --> 00:46:13,800
and its own neurotic attitudes and actions.

449
00:46:17,800 --> 00:46:21,800
So sex becomes important

450
00:46:21,800 --> 00:46:25,800
when everything else becomes unimportant.

451
00:46:27,800 --> 00:46:33,800
When life, the whole of it, not just sex,

452
00:46:36,800 --> 00:46:38,800
life includes living,

453
00:46:38,800 --> 00:46:43,800
life includes what love is, what death is,

454
00:46:46,800 --> 00:46:50,800
the whole movement of living.

455
00:46:51,800 --> 00:46:53,800
When that has no meaning,

456
00:46:53,800 --> 00:46:56,800
then one fragment which you call sex

457
00:46:56,800 --> 00:47:01,800
becomes extraordinarily important and vital.

458
00:47:01,800 --> 00:47:04,800
When you are not passionate

459
00:47:06,800 --> 00:47:09,800
about freedom inwardly,

460
00:47:09,800 --> 00:47:13,800
then you are lustfully passionate about sex.

461
00:47:13,800 --> 00:47:15,800
That's all.

462
00:47:17,800 --> 00:47:22,800
And with that you associate love,

463
00:47:22,800 --> 00:47:24,800
pleasure.

464
00:47:29,800 --> 00:47:35,800
And with that you associate tenderness,

465
00:47:35,800 --> 00:47:38,800
gentleness.

466
00:47:38,800 --> 00:47:44,800
You may be sexually very tender, very kind, considerate,

467
00:47:44,800 --> 00:47:46,800
but outwardly you destroy,

468
00:47:46,800 --> 00:47:48,800
you kill everything around you,

469
00:47:48,800 --> 00:47:54,800
animals to eat, to hunt.

470
00:47:57,800 --> 00:48:02,800
So your love is based on pleasure

471
00:48:02,800 --> 00:48:06,800
and therefore is it love?

472
00:48:11,800 --> 00:48:17,800
Love surely is something none of all this.

473
00:48:18,800 --> 00:48:23,800
Compassion means passion for everybody,

474
00:48:26,800 --> 00:48:31,800
not to your particular little desire.

475
00:48:39,800 --> 00:48:43,800
So, when you understand what disorder is,

476
00:48:43,800 --> 00:48:47,800
by observing very closely,

477
00:48:47,800 --> 00:48:51,800
out of that comes order.

478
00:48:52,800 --> 00:48:56,800
And order has its own discipline,

479
00:48:56,800 --> 00:48:59,800
which is its own virtue,

480
00:48:59,800 --> 00:49:06,800
and therefore that order is the supreme good

481
00:49:06,800 --> 00:49:08,800
and therefore love,

482
00:49:08,800 --> 00:49:14,800
which has nothing whatsoever to do with pleasure,

483
00:49:16,800 --> 00:49:20,800
because pleasure has pain.

484
00:49:22,800 --> 00:49:27,800
Love is enjoyment.

485
00:49:29,800 --> 00:49:32,800
Love is joy,

486
00:49:32,800 --> 00:49:37,800
not the purest thing that one man has made it.

487
00:49:39,800 --> 00:49:43,800
And to find that out, what love is,

488
00:49:43,800 --> 00:49:48,800
you must also understand what death is.

489
00:49:48,800 --> 00:49:51,800
Right?

490
00:49:52,800 --> 00:49:56,800
Do you really want to understand what death is?

491
00:49:56,800 --> 00:50:00,800
Yes? I doubt it.

492
00:50:02,800 --> 00:50:05,800
Very much.

493
00:50:06,800 --> 00:50:11,800
Because you are all so scared of death,

494
00:50:15,800 --> 00:50:18,800
aren't you?

495
00:50:19,800 --> 00:50:26,800
Or you have a belief in after-life,

496
00:50:26,800 --> 00:50:30,800
therefore you are not frightened.

497
00:50:30,800 --> 00:50:34,800
You have rationalised your life

498
00:50:36,800 --> 00:50:38,800
knowing that it is going to come to an end,

499
00:50:38,800 --> 00:50:42,800
the puny, shoddy little life that one lives,

500
00:50:42,800 --> 00:50:44,800
and if one is frightened of that,

501
00:50:44,800 --> 00:50:47,800
therefore we say, let's rationalise it,

502
00:50:47,800 --> 00:50:51,800
think about it, clarify it, you know, all the rest of it.

503
00:50:51,800 --> 00:50:56,800
Or you have a belief in after-life.

504
00:50:56,800 --> 00:51:01,800
The whole of Asia believes in after-life.

505
00:51:01,800 --> 00:51:06,800
Millions believe in reincarnation.

506
00:51:07,800 --> 00:51:12,800
But they never question what it is that incarnates.

507
00:51:18,800 --> 00:51:22,800
They believe that there is a permanent entity

508
00:51:22,800 --> 00:51:24,800
that is going to incarnate, and so on.

509
00:51:24,800 --> 00:51:28,800
I won't go into all that.

510
00:51:28,800 --> 00:51:31,800
If you believe in reincarnation,

511
00:51:31,800 --> 00:51:36,800
then what matters is how you live today.

512
00:51:36,800 --> 00:51:38,800
Right?

513
00:51:38,800 --> 00:51:42,800
Because you are going to pay for it next life.

514
00:51:44,800 --> 00:51:48,800
How you live, what you do, what you think,

515
00:51:48,800 --> 00:51:52,800
what your morality is.

516
00:51:53,800 --> 00:51:59,800
So, even though you may believe in reincarnation,

517
00:52:01,800 --> 00:52:05,800
what matters is how you live now.

518
00:52:06,800 --> 00:52:11,800
So you have to face death,

519
00:52:12,800 --> 00:52:17,800
not postponed it till old age,

520
00:52:17,800 --> 00:52:24,800
some accident, disease, and so on.

521
00:52:24,800 --> 00:52:28,800
You have to meet it, you have to understand it,

522
00:52:31,800 --> 00:52:35,800
not be afraid of it.

523
00:52:40,800 --> 00:52:46,800
So we say we must understand life

524
00:52:47,800 --> 00:52:49,800
and avoid death,

525
00:52:49,800 --> 00:52:54,800
but if you see life as a whole,

526
00:52:54,800 --> 00:52:57,800
in which there is this living

527
00:52:57,800 --> 00:53:02,800
and this extraordinary thing called love and death

528
00:53:02,800 --> 00:53:05,800
as a total unit,

529
00:53:05,800 --> 00:53:09,800
not three separate things,

530
00:53:11,800 --> 00:53:14,800
then what is death?

531
00:53:15,800 --> 00:53:22,800
The organism by usage, disease, and all the rest of it,

532
00:53:22,800 --> 00:53:25,800
comes to an end.

533
00:53:25,800 --> 00:53:29,800
It comes to an end quicker when there is conflict.

534
00:53:30,800 --> 00:53:33,800
All your heart failures and all the business of it

535
00:53:33,800 --> 00:53:36,800
is the result of this extraordinary emotional,

536
00:53:36,800 --> 00:53:39,800
contradictory way of living.

537
00:53:40,800 --> 00:53:44,800
The organism comes to an end.

538
00:53:46,800 --> 00:53:52,800
And either you can say, that's the end of it – finished.

539
00:53:55,800 --> 00:53:59,800
Or, which we don't say,

540
00:53:59,800 --> 00:54:06,800
the end of the whole structure and the nature of the me.

541
00:54:07,800 --> 00:54:14,800
The me, which has divided itself as us and they,

542
00:54:14,800 --> 00:54:18,800
we and those, we and you,

543
00:54:18,800 --> 00:54:24,800
that me is the centre of conflict.

544
00:54:30,800 --> 00:54:34,800
Now, can that me die?

545
00:54:37,800 --> 00:54:43,800
Not eventually, but every day.

546
00:54:44,800 --> 00:54:46,800
Then you will know what death is,

547
00:54:46,800 --> 00:54:50,800
so that the mind is always, tomorrow it is fresh

548
00:54:50,800 --> 00:54:54,800
because you have a death to the past.

549
00:54:54,800 --> 00:54:56,800
Are you following all this?

550
00:54:56,800 --> 00:55:01,800
No, sir, do it, not follow it.

551
00:55:02,800 --> 00:55:10,800
Die to your pleasure, die to your furniture.

552
00:55:10,800 --> 00:55:15,800
And that's what you are, your furniture,

553
00:55:15,800 --> 00:55:17,800
whether the chair or the furniture

554
00:55:17,800 --> 00:55:22,800
that you have accumulated in your mind,

555
00:55:22,800 --> 00:55:26,800
which you call knowledge,

556
00:55:26,800 --> 00:55:30,800
so that you die every day to everything

557
00:55:30,800 --> 00:55:34,800
that you have accumulated.

558
00:55:34,800 --> 00:55:39,800
And that's what's going to happen to you, anyhow.

559
00:55:42,800 --> 00:55:51,800
That means to empty the mind of everything known,

560
00:55:52,800 --> 00:55:58,800
which means the mind becomes utterly innocent.

561
00:56:01,800 --> 00:56:06,800
And it is only such a mind

562
00:56:06,800 --> 00:56:13,800
that has this extraordinary religious quality of purity

563
00:56:13,800 --> 00:56:21,800
that can come upon what is called enlightenment.

